# Every image in this project (bark-detector itself, and the test-rig
# publishers) builds/runs on Linux, but development happens on Windows too -
# a shell script checked out with CRLF line endings breaks its shebang
# (`#!/bin/sh\r` -> "no such file or directory") the moment it's baked into
# a container. Force LF regardless of platform/core.autocrlf so that can't
# happen again.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
